<% content_for :title, "On Mania | Bipolar Sober" %>

<style>
  .mania-page {
    background: #080808;
    color: #fff;
    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
  }

  .mania-page *,
  .mania-page *::before,
  .mania-page *::after {
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  .mania-hero {
    min-height: 85vh;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 80px 6%;
    background-color: #080808;
    background-image:
      linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(8, 8, 8, .55), transparent),
      url("<%= asset_path('bipolar_mania_desktop.png') %>");
    background-size: cover;
    background-position: center;
  }

  .mania-hero-content {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .mania-eyebrow {
    max-width: 440px;
    margin: 0 0 28px;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.6;
    letter-spacing: .12em;
  }

  .mania-hero h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(72px, 10vw, 150px);
    font-weight: 900;
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: .88;
    letter-spacing: -.065em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .mania-hero h1 span {
    display: block;
  }

  .mania-intro {
    margin: 32px 0 0;
    font-size: clamp(15px, 1.6vw, 22px);
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .mania-quote {
    padding: 48px 6%;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .mania-quote blockquote {
    max-width: 1000px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .mania-quote blockquote p {
    margin: 0 0 20px;
    color: #eaff00;
    font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 56px);
    font-weight: 900;
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .mania-quote cite {
    font-size: 14px;
    font-style: normal;
  }

  .mania-section {
    padding: 72px 6%;
  }

  .mania-section-inner {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, .85fr) minmax(0, 1.15fr);
    gap: 60px;
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .mania-number {
    margin: 0 0 22px;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: .12em;
  }

  .mania-section h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(36px, 4.5vw, 68px);
    font-weight: 900;
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: .95;
    letter-spacing: -.045em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .mania-copy {
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .mania-copy p {
    margin: 0 0 22px;
  }

  .mania-copy p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .mania-copy ul {
    margin: 0 0 24px;
    padding-left: 22px;
  }

  .mania-copy li {
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .mania-pink {
    background: #ff1493;
    color: #080808;
  }

  .mania-yellow {
    background: #eaff00;
    color: #080808;
  }

  .mania-purple {
    background: #8a00ff;
    color: #fff;
  }

  .mania-black {
    background: #080808;
    color: #fff;
  }

  .mania-white {
    background: #fff;
    color: #080808;
  }

  .mania-takeaway {
    padding-top: 22px;
    border-top: 3px solid currentColor;
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .mania-footer {
    padding: 40px 6%;
    border-top: 1px solid #444;
  }

  .mania-footer-inner {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 24px;
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .mania-footer a {
    color: #eaff00;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.5;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .mania-footer a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .mania-footer a:focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid #ff1493;
    outline-offset: 6px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .mania-hero {
      min-height: 88svh;
      align-items: flex-start;
      padding: 48px 6% 60px;
      background-image:
        url("<%= asset_path('bipolar_mania_mobile.png') %>");
      background-position: center bottom;
    }

    .mania-eyebrow {
      margin-bottom: 24px;
      font-size: 10px;
    }

    .mania-hero h1 {
      font-size: clamp(64px, 19vw, 108px);
    }

    .mania-intro {
      margin-top: 24px;
      font-size: 14px;
    }

    .mania-section {
      padding: 48px 6%;
    }

    .mania-section-inner {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 28px;
    }

    .mania-section h2 {
      font-size: clamp(36px, 10vw, 58px);
    }

    .mania-copy {
      font-size: 16px;
      line-height: 1.8;
    }

    .mania-number {
      margin-bottom: 16px;
    }
  }
</style>

<main class="mania-page">

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="mania-hero" aria-labelledby="mania-title">
    <div class="mania-hero-content">

      <p class="mania-eyebrow">
        BIPOLAR SOBER / BIPOLAR / MANIA
      </p>

      <h1 id="mania-title">
        <span>ON</span>
        <span>MANIA.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="mania-intro">
        THE IDEAS. THE URGENCY.<br>
        THE FUCK-ITS. THE SPENDING.<br>
        MAKING ROOM BEFORE YOU ACT.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- QUOTE -->
  <section class="mania-quote" aria-label="Opening quote">
    <blockquote>
      <p>“Boy, that escalated quickly.”</p>
      <cite>— Ron Burgundy</cite>
    </blockquote>
  </section>


  <!-- 01 / URGENCY -->
  <section class="mania-section mania-purple">
    <div class="mania-section-inner">

      <div class="mania-section-heading">
        <p class="mania-number">01 / EVERYTHING FEELS URGENT</p>

        <h2>
          BUY IT.<br>
          START IT.<br>
          RIGHT NOW.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="mania-copy">
        <p>
          Mania can shrink the space between an idea and an action.
          Buy something. Start a project. Change the plan.
          Consequences that usually matter feel distant, and this
          decision seems completely reasonable.
        </p>

        <p>
          For you, overspending and impulsivity are a huge part of it.
          You take your medication and want stability. You also know
          what it means to get the fuck-its and act before considering
          what comes next.
        </p>

        <p class="mania-takeaway">
          Wanting to manage your illness and struggling during an
          episode can both be true. You deserve compassion and
          a practical plan.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 02 / OVERSPENDING -->
  <section class="mania-section mania-yellow">
    <div class="mania-section-inner">

      <div class="mania-section-heading">
        <p class="mania-number">02 / THE CART KEEPS GROWING</p>

        <h2>
          YOUR BUDGET<br>
          DESERVES<br>
          A SAY.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="mania-copy">
        <p>
          You need it. It is useful. It is an investment.
          You will figure out the money later. Each purchase
          sounds reasonable on its own while the total keeps growing.
          Even a project you genuinely care about can become
          an urgent reason to spend.
        </p>

        <p>
          Notice the excitement, the explanation, and the discomfort
          of leaving something alone. What do you expect the purchase
          to provide: enjoyment, relief, a fresh start?
          Understanding desire gives you room to examine it.
        </p>

        <p>
          “I can afford it” means checking your actual finances.
          “I need it today” means asking what happens if you wait.
          Your future self has the same bills and deserves
          consideration now.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 03 / SAFEGUARDS -->
  <section class="mania-section mania-pink">
    <div class="mania-section-inner">

      <div class="mania-section-heading">
        <p class="mania-number">03 / PLAN WHILE YOU CAN</p>

        <h2>
          GIVE THE<br>
          IDEA SOME<br>
          SPACE.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="mania-copy">
        <p>
          Build safeguards before your priorities start shifting.
          Choose limits you are willing to use and people you trust
          to help you assess decisions.
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>Remove saved payment information and set spending alerts.</li>
          <li>Give larger purchases a waiting period or a trusted second opinion.</li>
          <li>Step away from browsing when it keeps turning into buying.</li>
          <li>Write ideas down before turning them into commitments.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          Everything can feel possible at once. Letting an idea
          exist overnight gives you another chance to consider
          the money, time, and obligations it would require.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 04 / DESIRE AND LIMITS -->
  <section class="mania-section mania-black">
    <div class="mania-section-inner">

      <div class="mania-section-heading">
        <p class="mania-number">04 / PRACTICE THE PAUSE</p>

        <h2>
          CAN YOU<br>
          LET IT<br>
          WAIT?
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="mania-copy">
        <p>
          Treat waiting as a challenge in resourcefulness.
          Can you leave the item in the cart? Let the plan sit?
          Allow someone else to help assess it?
          Give yourself credit for making space around the urge.
        </p>

        <p>
          One part of you wants freedom, excitement, and immediate
          action. Another wants stability, sobriety, and money for
          necessities. Get curious about both. What feels unbearable
          about waiting? What are you hoping to gain?
        </p>

        <p class="mania-takeaway">
          You can care about the part that wants everything right
          now while protecting your choices for tomorrow.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 05 / SUPPORT -->
  <section class="mania-section mania-white">
    <div class="mania-section-inner">

      <div class="mania-section-heading">
        <p class="mania-number">05 / MAKE ROOM FOR SUPPORT</p>

        <h2>
          YOU DON’T<br>
          HAVE TO<br>
          ASSESS IT<br>
          ALONE.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="mania-copy">
        <p>
          You cannot guarantee that every episode will be prevented.
          You can prepare by knowing your patterns, protecting
          essential money, and deciding who can help when your
          judgment changes. An episode does not erase those efforts.
        </p>

        <p>
          Your experience of mania can also involve psychosis.
          Include that in your treatment plan, even when spending
          and impulsivity are the changes you notice first.
          If experiences or beliefs become unusual, or trusted
          people notice concerning changes, involve your treatment
          team promptly.
        </p>

        <p>
          Support belongs in the plan for the times when pausing
          and evaluating decisions become difficult.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 06 / AFTERWARD -->
  <section class="mania-section mania-yellow">
    <div class="mania-section-inner">

      <div class="mania-section-heading">
        <p class="mania-number">06 / REPAIR WITHOUT SELF-DESTRUCTION</p>

        <h2>
          FACE THE<br>
          AFTERMATH.<br>
          KEEP YOUR<br>
          DIGNITY.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="mania-copy">
        <p>
          Looking at the purchases and commitments afterward can
          feel overwhelming. Start with what needs attention.
          Return or cancel what you can, review obligations,
          and ask for help with the rest. You do not have to
          resolve everything in one sitting.
        </p>

        <p>
          “I spent money I needed” identifies something to address.
          “I ruin everything” turns it into your identity.
          Accountability gives you a place to begin repairing
          and preparing.
        </p>

        <p class="mania-takeaway">
          You are more than an episode or a decision you regret.
          Keep building room to choose and support for the times
          when choosing becomes difficult.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- NAVIGATION -->
  <nav class="mania-footer" aria-label="Bipolar topic navigation">
    <div class="mania-footer-inner">
      <%= link_to "← BACK TO BIPOLAR", bipolar_path %>
      <%= link_to "NEXT: ON DEPRESSION →", bipolar_depression_path %>
    </div>
  </nav>

</main>